\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Continued pretraining on identical bytes per arm (one seed). BPB: bits per byte on held-out native text split into ${\sim }$2{,}000-byte pieces (primary metric) and on FLORES-200 devtest. Belebele: zero-shot accuracy (900 items, chance 0.25), scored on answer text. chrF++: 5-shot FLORES-200 devtest translation. Gen.\ B/s: UTF-8 bytes of Nepali generated per second (batch 64, greedy). Tokens: training tokens seen (for B1, excluding the embedding warm-up on the first 10\% of the same stream). Bold: best Nepali BPB within each block. All BPB here use the registered prefix; the B1 Llama rows are dominated by the scoring artifact of \S  \ref  {sec:cpt}, and Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:prefix} gives the training-separator comparison.\relax }}{17}{table.caption.61}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:cpt}{{8}{17}{Continued pretraining on identical bytes per arm (one seed). BPB: bits per byte on held-out native text split into ${\sim }$2{,}000-byte pieces (primary metric) and on FLORES-200 devtest. Belebele: zero-shot accuracy (900 items, chance 0.25), scored on answer text. chrF++: 5-shot FLORES-200 devtest translation. Gen.\ B/s: UTF-8 bytes of Nepali generated per second (batch 64, greedy). Tokens: training tokens seen (for B1, excluding the embedding warm-up on the first 10\% of the same stream). Bold: best Nepali BPB within each block. All BPB here use the registered prefix; the B1 Llama rows are dominated by the scoring artifact of \S \ref {sec:cpt}, and Table~\ref {tab:prefix} gives the training-separator comparison.\relax }{table.caption.61}{}}
